.TH man 7 "31 Dec 2024" "v4" "ldmsd_stream_publish_iterator man page"

.SH NAME
dynamic_query_client_server - man page for the dynamic_query_client/server utilities


.SH SYNOPSIS

.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a test code to be used with the dynamic stream sampler. This will be the basis
of a code that might call and action on the database and then send that info the dynamic stream.
It is based on ldmsd_stream_publisher.

dynamic_query_client - sends a query tag to the dynamic_query_server which is listening on a port

dynamic_query_server - listens on a port for a query tag. Based on the tag, it fake makes a call and then
sends the fake result down the newly created dynamic stream.

.SH CONFIGURATION ATTRIBUTE SYNTAX - CLIENT
.TP
.BR command line argv
<query tag>
.br
query to be sent
.RE

.SH CONFIGURATION ATTRIBUTE SYNTAX - SERVER
.TP
.BR host
-h <hostname>
.br
hostname of the ldmsd it will send the response to

.BR port
-p <port>
.br
port of the ldmsd it will send the response to

.BR auth
-a <auth>
.br
auth of the ldmsd it will send the response to (think there are other flags related to auth as well)

.BR stream
-s <dynamic_stream>
.br
stream to which it will publish on the ldmsd

.BR HARDWIRED PORT
.br
there is a hardwired port 53000 which is the port on which this receives query messages

.RE

.SH BUGS
This is underdevelopment and is not guarenteed to work and is subject to change without notice

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Assuming hosts on ports 52001, 52002, and 52003 have been started and they have loaded the dynamic_stream_sampler configured like:
.nf
load name=dynamic_stream_sampler
config name=dynamic_stream_sampler producer=host1 instance=host1/hello_sampler stream=cmd_stream52001 component_id=1
start name=dynamic_stream_sampler interval=2000000 offset=0

Setup the dynamic stream via:
.nf
 ./ldmsd_stream_publish -x sock -p 52001 -s cmd_stream52001 -t json -a munge -f /home/gentile/Work/Build/streams/cmdstream.in -h localhost

.nf
cat cmdstream.in
{"cmd" : "SETUP_FEEDBACK", "stream" : "dynamicbar", "prdcrname" : "zedprdcr", "list" : "localhost@52001@cmd_stream52001:localhost@52002@cmd_stream52002:localhost@52003@cmd_stream52003"}

.nf
Start the server via:
.nf
 ./dynamic_query_server -x sock -p 52003 -s dynamicbar -a munge -h localhost
.nf

Start the client via:
.nf
 ./dynamic_query_client QUERY_1
.nf

.nf
and the server will sfke do the query and send a fake result down the dynamicbar stream
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
ldmsd_stream_publish(7), Plugin_dynamic_stream_sampler(7)
